    "linkedin:3a4db5851c3299f2a5d7964c": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Full Stack Engineer Intern",
        "company": "ByteShifted",
        "location": "Islamabad, Islāmābād, Pakistan",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465232555",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "**Company Description** \n\n\n\n\n ByteShifted is a technology solutions company focused on delivering innovative, reliable, and scalable software for organizations of all sizes. The team partners closely with clients to understand their goals, challenges, and vision, then designs solutions that fit seamlessly into existing operations. Services include custom software development, web and mobile applications, automation and AI, cloud solutions, system integration, and UI/UX design. ByteShifted emphasizes transparent collaboration, long\\-term relationships, and measurable business outcomes such as increased productivity, reduced costs, and successful product launches. Applicants can expect to join a customer\\-first environment that values agility, clear communication, and continuous improvement.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Role Description** \n\n\n\n\n The Software Engineer Intern role at ByteShifted is a full\\-time, remote position focused on supporting the development of software solutions for client projects. Day\\-to\\-day tasks include implementing and testing backend functionality, assisting in building and maintaining web services, and writing clean, maintainable code under the guidance of senior engineers. The intern will help debug and resolve technical issues, contribute to code reviews, and participate in agile ceremonies such as stand\\-ups or sprint planning. This role also involves documenting technical work, collaborating with cross\\-functional team members, and learning modern tools, frameworks, and development practices within a professional engineering environment.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Qualifications** \n\n\n\n* Strong foundation in Computer Science concepts such as data structures, algorithms, and software design principles.\n* Skills in Software Development and Programming, with experience in at least one modern language (e.g., Java, Python, JavaScript, C\\#, or similar).\n* Knowledge of Back\\-End Web Development, including APIs, databases, and server\\-side frameworks.\n* Understanding of Object\\-Oriented Programming (OOP) and ability to apply OOP principles in practical projects.\n* Currently pursuing or recently completed a degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n* Familiarity with version control systems (e.g., Git) and collaborative development workflows.\n* Ability to work independently in a remote setting, manage time effectively, and communicate clearly with distributed teams.\n* Interest in modern software practices such as testing, code reviews, and agile methodologies; prior project or internship experience is a plus.",
