        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "**Company Description** \n UplynkTech is a custom software development company that builds web and mobile applications, AI\\-powered solutions, digital marketing platforms, and tailor\\-made ERP systems. The company focuses on creating scalable, high\\-performance digital products for schools, hospitals, wholesale businesses, and a variety of other sectors. UplynkTech helps organizations streamline operations, automate workflows, and support sustainable growth through innovative technology. By combining engineering excellence with data\\-driven digital strategies, the team delivers solutions that improve efficiency, decision\\-making, and user experiences.\n   \n\n**Role Description** \n This is a full\\-time remote role for a TypeScript Developer. The TypeScript Developer will design, implement, and maintain back\\-end and front\\-end application features using TypeScript and related frameworks. Daily responsibilities include writing clean, testable code, reviewing peer code, debugging and resolving issues, and collaborating with product and design teams to translate requirements into technical solutions. The role involves integrating APIs, optimizing performance, maintaining documentation, and participating in agile ceremonies such as stand\\-ups and sprint planning. The developer will work closely with other engineers to ensure scalability, security, and reliability across UplynkTech’s software products.\n   \n\n**Qualifications**\n  \n\n* Strong foundation in Computer Science, including algorithms, data structures, and software design principles.\n* Experience in Back\\-End Web Development and Software Development, with a focus on building scalable, secure services.\n* Proficiency in Programming and Object\\-Oriented Programming (OOP), preferably with TypeScript and JavaScript.\n* Hands\\-on experience with modern web frameworks (e.g., Node.js, NestJS, React or similar), RESTful APIs, and relational or NoSQL databases.\n* Familiarity with version control systems (e.g., Git), CI/CD pipelines, and automated testing practices.\n* Ability to work independently in a remote environment, manage priorities, and collaborate effectively within cross\\-functional teams.\n* Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related field, or equivalent practical experience.\n* Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, GCP) and containerization (e.g., Docker) is a strong plus.",
